   "etymology": "Multiple etymologies:\n*From Proto-Albanian *dȫgā-, from Pre-Proto-Albanian *d(u̯)ōgā, from Proto-Indo-European *du̯oi̯gʰ(h₁)e-h₂- (“forking”), from older Proto-Indo-European *du̯i-gʰh₁-ó-, from *dwi-.\n*Identical as above, but alternatively reconstructed as Proto-Albanian *dēgā- < Pre-Proto-Albanian *d(u̯)ai̯g⁽ʰ⁾ā-.\n*From Proto-Albanian *duaigā, from Proto-Indo-European *dwoy-, from the root *dwi- (“binary, consisting of two”). Cognate to Old High German zwig (“forking, crotch (of tree); bough, branch”).\n*From a root *deh₃gʰ- shared with Proto-Germanic *tōgô (“branch”).",
